{
  "format": "tnca-tilebench-coverage/1",
  "source": "https://github.com/Deep-Learning-Profiling-Tools/Tilebench",
  "about": [
    "The 45 operators TileBench defines, and whether this compiler can build",
    "each one from Triton source.",
    "",
    "The goal is coverage with the KERNEL UNCHANGED. A operator that only",
    "compiles after its Triton source is rewritten to avoid something we do",
    "not support has not been covered; it has been avoided. So each entry",
    "records the kernel actually compiled and, when it fails, the exact",
    "diagnostic -- not a category.",
    "",
    "`kernel: null` means no representative kernel has been written yet. That",
    "is NOT RUN, and it is counted apart from failures: a suite that quietly",
    "omitted the hard operators would report a coverage number that means",
    "nothing."
  ],
